  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Cyclohexanone may be a target of Jurkat through multiple pathways, with HEp-2 as a common intermediate in these relationships. HEp-2 is identified as a target of both 3,4,5-trihydroxy-8-[(2R,3S)-3,5,7-trihydroxy-3,4-dihydro-2H-chromen-2-yl]-1-[(2S,3S)-3,5,7-trihydroxy-3,4-dihydro-2H-chromen-2-yl]benzo[7]annulen-6-one and (1R,2S,5R,6R,7S,8R)-8-hydroperoxy-1,5-dimethyl-8-prop-1-en-2-yltricyclo[5.3.0.02,6]decane, both of which target Jurkat. Additionally, Cyclohexanone is linked to HEp-2 and subsequently to Jurkat through the pathway involving Tatridin B. These findings collectively suggest that Cyclohexanone may exert its biological effects via a series of molecular interactions that ultimately lead to the targeting of Jurkat. The evidence is consistent across different pathways, indicating a potential mechanism involving the interaction of Cyclohexanone with cellular targets that are subsequently engaged by other compounds, which in turn affect Jurkat. The strength of the evidence is supported by multiple high-scoring paths, but the exact nature of the interaction between Cyclohexanone and Jurkat remains partially uncertain, as the direct mechanism of action is not fully elucidated.",
